From a23d30f7dafeeb0c2d40367a28a8fff922509de7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Lasso <lasso@queensu.ca>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:52:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ENH: Show binary labelmap segmentations as smooth surfaces in
 3D views

Experimental display mode: when the representation in 3D views of a
segmentation is "Binary labelmap", the segmentations displayable manager
shows the labelmap as smooth surfaces computed on the GPU, without
converting it to closed surface. Based on pieper/SlicerLive.

vtkSegmentationLabelmapSurfaceMapper computes a signed distance field of
the shown segments in fragment shader passes (jump flooding), smooths it
(Gaussian with twicing, which keeps thin structures; narrow gaps between
segments are filled), and ray casts its zero level set. Works with
OpenGL and WebGL2 (requires EXT_color_buffer_float).

- Opaque segments share one surface with soft color seams, each
  translucent segment has its own (depth peeling and order independent
  translucency are supported).
- Clipping (union and intersection clip types) with caps and outline,
  per-segment 3D opacity and visibility, lighting,
  shadows (screen-space ambient occlusion).
- Picking: vtkMRMLAccuratePicker asks the mapper to intersect the ray
  (new IntersectRayEvent), so Shift+mouse move, Pick3D and painting in
  3D views work on these surfaces.
- Editing updates the distance field only around the changed labels.
- Non-linear transforms: the labelmap is resampled on the CPU.
- Large labelmaps are downsampled to MaximumNumberOfVoxels.
- The surface smoothing factor conversion parameter sets the smoothing.

Show 3D button: new "Representation" submenu (binary labelmap or closed
surface), the same choice as the Segmentations module's representation
in 3D views. Show 3D only creates the chosen representation and does
not switch to closed surface. The default representation in 3D views
for new segmentations can be set in application settings
(Segmentations/DefaultRepresentation3D; default remains closed surface).
